      "code": "CUSTOM !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n  mobile itou.......",
      "status": "",
      "output": "<p>CUSTOM !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n  mobile itou.......</p>\n",
      "type": "html"
    },
    {
      "code": "Welcome to Scribbler\n====================\n\nA Javascript Compiler and Notebook Tool\n--------------------------\n\n[Gallery](https://scribbler.live/samples.html) Ã¢ÂÂ¢ [Tutorials](https://scribbler.live/tutorials) Ã¢ÂÂ¢ [Docs](https://scribbler.live/docs) Ã¢ÂÂ¢ [Discussions](https://github.com/gopi-suvanam/scribbler/discussions/) Ã¢ÂÂ¢ [Github](https://github.com/gopi-suvanam/scribbler/)\n\n* * *\n\t\t  \n\n### Double-click this cell to edit\n\nScribbler is an interactive environment for experimenting in javascript using a simple interface (without servers and backend deployment) - essentially an easy-to-use online compiler. Scribbler can be used for:\n\n*   Scientific Computation\n*   Data Science/Machine Learning\n*   Dashboard Development\n*   Experimenting With new Code/Libraries\n\nPlease feel free to send in pull requests/issues on Github. Next few cells give you the \"hello world\" notebook.\n\n\n\n\n   ",
      "status": "",
      "output": "<h1>Welcome to Scribbler</h1>\n<h2>A Javascript Compiler and Notebook Tool</h2>\n<p><a href=\"https://scribbler.live/samples.html\">Gallery</a> Ã¢ÂÂ¢ <a href=\"https://scribbler.live/tutorials\">Tutorials</a> Ã¢ÂÂ¢ <a href=\"https://scribbler.live/docs\">Docs</a> Ã¢ÂÂ¢ <a href=\"https://github.com/gopi-suvanam/scribbler/discussions/\">Discussions</a> Ã¢ÂÂ¢ <a href=\"https://github.com/gopi-suvanam/scribbler/\">Github</a></p>\n<hr>\n<h3>Double-click this cell to edit</h3>\n<p>Scribbler is an interactive environment for experimenting in javascript using a simple interface (without servers and backend deployment) - essentially an easy-to-use online compiler. Scribbler can be used for:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Scientific Computation</li>\n<li>Data Science/Machine Learning</li>\n<li>Dashboard Development</li>\n<li>Experimenting With new Code/Libraries</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Please feel free to send in pull requests/issues on Github. Next few cells give you the \"hello world\" notebook.</p>\n",
      "type": "html"
    },
    {
      "code": "#### To start with, you could simply do: ",
      "status": "",
      "output": "<h4>To start with, you could simply do:</h4>\n",
      "type": "html"
    },
    {
      "code": "scrib.show(\"Hello World\") //Edit the text and press the play button to see the change in the next cell",
      "status": "[1]<br><span style=\"font-size:8px\">0ms<span></span></span>",
      "output": "Hello World <br>",
      "type": "code"
    },
    {
      "code": "//> html\n<b> You can use HTML also by putting <i>//> html</i>. </b>\n\n<br>\n<a href=\"scirbbler.live\" targe=\"_blank\">Scribbler website </a>",
      "status": "[2]<br><span style=\"font-size:8px\">0ms<span></span></span>",
      "output": "\n<b> You can use HTML also by putting <i>//&gt; html</i>. </b>\n\n<br>\n<a href=\"scirbbler.live\" targe=\"_blank\">Scribbler website </a> <br>",
      "type": "code"
    },
    {
      "code": "#### Or to show off you could write a function to do that.",
      "status": "",
      "output": "<h4>Or to show off you could write a function to do that.</h4>\n",
      "type": "html"
    },
    {
      "code": "function greet(who){\n   scrib.show(\"Hello \"+who); \n}\ngreet(\"world\")",
      "status": "[3]<br><span style=\"font-size:8px\">0ms<span></span></span>",
      "output": "Hello world <br>",
      "type": "code"
    },
    {
      "code": "#### And of course you can make the world greener! ",
      "status": "",
      "output": "<h4>And of course you can make the world greener!</h4>\n",
      "type": "html"
    },
    {
      "code": "greet('<span style=\"background-color:green;color:white\">World</span>')",
      "status": "[4]<br><span style=\"font-size:8px\">0ms<span></span></span>",
      "output": "Hello <span style=\"background-color:green;color:white\">World</span> <br>",
      "type": "code"
    },
    {
      "code": "## Working with Cells\nScribbler notebooks have two types of cells: \n- an html cell, the cell you are reading right now. \n- a code cell, where you may input some JS code for the browser to execute. \n\n New cells can be added (Ã¢ÂÂ/Option-Enter), deleted (Ã¢ÂÂ), moved up (Ã¢ÂÂ²), moved down (Ã¢ÂÂ¼) using the menu on the top right corner of the cell. The cell type can be toggled between html and code as well. \n A code cell can be run using the run button (Ã¢ÂÂº) or the keyboard shortcut: Ctrl-Enter/Shift-Enter.\n\n Double click on this cell to edit the html. You can download the notebook as a json object to load it later or you can download it as a static html. \nFor more details checkout the [Docs](https://github.com/gopi-suvanam/jsnb/blob/main/DOCS.md).  ",
      "status": "",
      "output": "<h2>Working with Cells</h2>\n<p>Scribbler notebooks have two types of cells: </p>\n<ul>\n<li>an html cell, the cell you are reading right now. </li>\n<li>a code cell, where you may input some JS code for the browser to execute.</li>\n</ul>\n<p> New cells can be added (Ã¢ÂÂ/Option-Enter), deleted (Ã¢ÂÂ), moved up (Ã¢ÂÂ²), moved down (Ã¢ÂÂ¼) using the menu on the top right corner of the cell. The cell type can be toggled between html and code as well. \n A code cell can be run using the run button (Ã¢ÂÂº) or the keyboard shortcut: Ctrl-Enter/Shift-Enter.</p>\n<p> Double click on this cell to edit the html. You can download the notebook as a json object to load it later or you can download it as a static html. \nFor more details checkout the <a href=\"https://github.com/gopi-suvanam/jsnb/blob/main/DOCS.md\">Docs</a>.  </p>\n",
      "type": "html"
    },
    {
      "code": "//>md\n## Math and Plotting\nYou can use all JS functionality in a sandboxed environment easily. Next cell shows illustrates use of array function and plotting of a chart.",
      "status": "",
      "output": "<h2>Math and Plotting</h2>\n<p>You can use all JS functionality in a sandboxed environment easily. Next cell shows illustrates use of array function and plotting of a chart.</p>\n",
      "type": "html"
    },
    {
      "code": "var id=range(1,10,0.01).map(Math.sin).plot();",
